Sec. 60001. This section rescinds the unobligated balances of funds made available to carry out section 132 of the Clean Air Act (42 U.S.C. 7432), which pertains to clean heavy-duty vehicles.

Sec. 60002. Section 134 of the Clean Air Act (42 U.S.C. 7434), establishing the Greenhouse Gas Reduction Fund, is repealed. Additionally, the unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out that section are rescinded.

Sec. 60003. The unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 60104 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2067) are rescinded. This action eliminates remaining funding for diesel emissions reductions.

Sec. 60004. The unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 60105 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2067) are rescinded. This rescinds funding designated to address general air pollution.

Sec. 60005. The unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 60106 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2069) are rescinded. This eliminates remaining funds for addressing air pollution specifically at schools.

Sec. 60006. The unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 135 of the Clean Air Act (42 U.S.C. 7435) are rescinded. This action terminates funding for the low emissions electricity program.

Sec. 60007. The unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 60108 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2070) are rescinded. This rescinds funding associated with section 211(o) of the Clean Air Act.

Sec. 60008. The unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 60109 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2071) are rescinded. This eliminates remaining funds for the implementation of the American Innovation and Manufacturing Act.

Sec. 60009. The unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 60110 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2071) are rescinded. This rescinds funding for enforcement technology and public information initiatives.

Sec. 60010. The unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 60111 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2072) are rescinded. This action eliminates remaining funds for greenhouse gas corporate reporting.

Sec. 60011. The unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 60112 of Public Law 117-169 (42 U.S.C. 4321 note; 136 Stat. 2072) are rescinded. This rescinds funding for environmental product declaration assistance.

Sec. 60012. The unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out subsections (a) and (b) of section 136 of the Clean Air Act (42 U.S.C. 7436) are rescinded. Additionally, section 136(g) of the Clean Air Act is amended to extend the period from calendar year 2024 to calendar year 2034.

Sec. 60013. The unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 137 of the Clean Air Act (42 U.S.C. 7437) are rescinded. This eliminates remaining funds for greenhouse gas air pollution plans and implementation grants.

Sec. 60014. The unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 60115 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2077) are rescinded. This rescinds funding for the Environmental Protection Agency’s efficient, accurate, and timely reviews.

Sec. 60015. The unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 60116 of Public Law 117-169 (42 U.S.C. 4321 note; 136 Stat. 2077) are rescinded. This action eliminates remaining funds for low-embodied carbon labeling for construction materials.

Sec. 60016. The unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 138 of the Clean Air Act (42 U.S.C. 7438) are rescinded. This rescinds funding for environmental and climate justice block grants.

Sec. 60017. The unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 60301 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2079) are rescinded. This eliminates remaining funds for Endangered Species Act recovery plans.

Sec. 60018. The unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 60401 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2079) are rescinded. This rescinds funding for environmental and climate data collection.

Sec. 60019. The unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 177 of title 23, United States Code, are rescinded. This action terminates the Neighborhood Access and Equity Grant Program.

Sec. 60020. The unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 60502 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2083) are rescinded. This rescinds funding for Federal building assistance.

Sec. 60021. The unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 60503 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2083) are rescinded. This eliminates remaining funds for low-carbon materials for Federal buildings.

Sec. 60022. The unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 60504 of Public Law 117-169 (136 Stat. 2083) are rescinded. This rescinds funding for GSA emerging and sustainable technologies.

Sec. 60023. The unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 178 of title 23, United States Code, are rescinded. This action eliminates remaining funds for environmental review implementation.

Sec. 60024. The unobligated balances of amounts made available to carry out section 179 of title 23, United States Code, are rescinded. This rescinds funding for low-carbon transportation materials grants.

Sec. 60025. This section appropriates $256,657,000 for fiscal year 2025, out of any money in the Treasury not otherwise appropriated, for the John F. Kennedy Center for the Performing Arts. The funds remain available until September 30, 2029, for capital repair, restoration, maintenance backlog, and security structures, with no more than 3 percent usable for administrative costs.

Sec. 60026. This section amends the National Environmental Policy Act of 1969 to allow project sponsors to pay fees for the preparation or supervision of environmental assessments or impact statements. The fee is set at 125 percent of the anticipated costs, and payment triggers strict deadlines: 180 days for environmental assessments and one year for environmental impact statements. [end of text]


